<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National People's Power</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2019">2019</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National People's Power is a left-wing political alliance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> formed in 2019 around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janatha-vimukthi-peramuna">Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna</a> together with trade unions, professional and civil-society groups. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anura-kumara-dissanayake">Anura Kumara Dissanayake</a>, it grew after the economic crisis and protests of 2022 by campaigning against corruption and the established parties. In 2024 its leader won the presidency and the alliance took a two-thirds majority in parliament.</p></div>
